  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TKAJ Pacific Digital Economy Programme (PDEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific Digital Economy Programme (PDEP) is a joint programme between UNCDF, UNDP and UN Trade &amp; Development (UNCTAD), implementated in Fiji, Tonga, Vanuatu, Samoa, Solomon Islands, Papua New Guinea, Timor-Leste, Kiribati, Federated States of Micronesia, and the Marshall Islands with the financial support of the governments of Australia and New Zealand as well as the European Union. The programme aims to foster inclusive digital economies in the Pacific that support rural communities, women and micro, small and medium-sized enterprises. It also supports the Forum Secretariat and the region with the implementation and coordination of the Pacific Regional E-commerce Strategy and Roadmap, and supports the Pacific E-commerce Initiative.</narrative>
  </description>
